"Future development of HKU Public Opinion Programme announced (2019-04-23, 홍콩대 민의연구계획의 독립 발표)","https://hkupop.pori.hk/english/release/release1583_pr.html","research"],["HKPORI","香港民研推出新網站及客席專欄 HKPORI Launches New Website and Guest Columns (2025-01-09, 새 누리집 안내)","https://www.pori.hk/article/press-release-2025-01-09","research"]],"note":"홍콩민의연구소는 2025년 1월 새 누리집으로 옮기면서 무료 자료 공개를 멈췄고, 공개 표는 2024년 11월 조사에서 끝난다.","note_en":"When HKPORI moved to a new website in January 2025 it stopped offering free data, and the public table ends with the November 2024 survey."}],"events":[{"d":"2003-07-01","pre":"2003-06-04","post":"2003-07-04","dir":"down","t":"기본법 23조 입법 반대 대행진","t_en":"Mass march against Article 23 legislation","x":"홍콩 기본법 23조는 반역·국가 분열·선동·중앙정부 전복·국가 기밀 절취를 금지하는 법을 홍콩이 스스로 만들도록 정해 두었다. 2003년 7월 1일 이 입법에 반대하는 대규모 시위가 열렸다. 홍콩중문대 천타오원 교수와 홍콩대 민의연구계획 중팅야오 주임의 공동 발표문은 50만 명이 거리로 나왔다고 적고, 행진 참가자 1,154명 조사에서 약 90%가 23조 입법 반대를, 80% 남짓이 둥젠화 퇴진을 꼽았다며 이 행진을 둥젠화에 대한 불신임 투표로 봤다. 그를 행정장관으로 뽑겠다는 응답은 6월 초 21%에서 7월 초 13%로 떨어졌다.","x_en":"Article 23 of Hong Kong's Basic Law requires the territory to enact its own laws prohibiting treason, secession, sedition, subversion against the Central People's Government and theft of state secrets. On 1 July 2003 a mass protest was held against such legislation. A joint release by Professor Joseph Chan of the Chinese University of Hong Kong and Robert Chung, director of the HKU Public Opinion Programme, said 500,000 people took to the streets; in their survey of 1,154 marchers about 90% said they marched to oppose the Article 23 law and just over 80% said Tung should step down, and they described the march as a vote of no confidence in him. The share who would vote for Tung fell from 21% in early June to 13% in early July.","src":[["HKUPOP","陳韜文·鍾庭耀 聯合新聞公報「調查發現：7.1遊行目的明確 參與者多屬中產階層」(2003-07-06, 7·1 행진 참가자 조사)","https://hkupop.pori.hk/english/resources/bl23/71/6%20July%2003.pdf","research"],["Basic Law","The Basic Law — Chapter II, Article 23 (홍콩 기본법 제2장 23조)","https://www.basiclaw.gov.hk/en/basiclaw/chapter2.html","official"],["HKUPOP","Hypothetical voting on Tung Chee-hwa as CE (per poll) (둥젠화 가상 투표 표)","https://hkupop.pori.hk/english/popexpress/ceall/cevote/poll/datatables1.html","research"]]},{"d":"2019-06","pre":"2019-06-04","post":"2019-06-18","dir":"down","t":"범죄인 인도 조례 개정 반대 시위","t_en":"Protests against the extradition bill","x":"2019년 캐리 람 정부는 홍콩 사람도 중국 본토로 넘겨 재판받게 할 수 있도록 도주범 조례를 고치려 했다. 학자 단체 의뢰로 홍콩대 민의연구계획이 5월 말~6월 초 한 조사에서 66%가 홍콩 사람을 본토로 넘겨 재판받게 하는 데 반대했다(찬성 17%). 6월 집회와 시위가 커지자 민의연구계획은 6월 25일 마지막 발표에서 '개정안을 둘러싼 집회·시위와 논란이 여론에 상당히 큰 영향을 준 것 같다'며 람의 지지가 23%, 반대가 67%로 취임 뒤 가장 나빠졌다고 적었다. 시위가 이어진 11월에는 지지 10%, 반대 82%까지 내려갔다.","x_en":"In 2019 Carrie Lam's government sought to amend the Fugitive Offenders Ordinance so that Hong Kong people could be sent to mainland China for trial. In a survey the HKU Public Opinion Programme conducted in late May and early June for a scholars' group, 66% opposed extraditing Hong Kong people to the mainland for trial (17% supported it). As rallies and protests grew in June, the programme wrote in its final release on 25 June that 'the rallies, protests and related controversies as a result of the amendments of the extradition bill appear to have affected public opinion to a fairly large extent', with Lam's support at 23% and opposition at 67%, her worst since taking office. As protests continued, support fell to 10% and opposition rose to 82% in November.","src":[["HKUPOP","HKU POP farewell release: Public sentiment plunges, CE popularity falls below the lowest benchmark (2019-06-25, 홍콩대 민의연구계획 마지막 발표)","https://hkupop.pori.hk/english/release/release1593.html","research"],["HKUPOP","Press Release: Public Opinion Poll on the 'Fugitive Offenders Ordinance' Amendment (도주범 조례 개정 여론조사, 2019-06)","https://hkupop.pori.hk/english/report/singming_extradition_bill/content/Survey%20release%20bilingual.pdf","research"],["HKPORI","Hypothetical Voting Results for Carrie Lam as the Chief Executive (캐리 람 가상 투표 표)","https://a2024.pori.hk/pop-poll/chief-executive/past-chief-executive/a003-app.html","research"]]}]}